Android USB fd-handoff for the dye-sub (DNP) backend.

On Android a non-root process cannot enumerate/open USB via usbfs. The app opens
the USB device through android.hardware.usb.UsbManager
(UsbDeviceConnection.getFileDescriptor()) and hands the raw fd to this backend.
libusb's supported mechanism is:

    libusb_set_option(NULL, LIBUSB_OPTION_NO_DEVICE_DISCOVERY);  // before libusb_init
    libusb_wrap_sys_device(NULL, (intptr_t)fd, &handle);         // wrap the app fd

NO_DEVICE_DISCOVERY MUST be set BEFORE libusb_init(): on unrooted Android,
libusb_init() otherwise scans /dev/bus/usb (usbfs), has no permission, and
returns -1 ("Failed to initialize libusb (-1)"). So the fd-get + NO_DEVICE_
DISCOVERY block runs immediately BEFORE libusb_init(NULL), and the single
printing_ffi_fd declaration is in scope for the later wrap path too.

Because cupsd starts BEFORE the USB device is plugged/opened, the fd must be
delivered at job time. Primary transport: SCM_RIGHTS over an AF_UNIX socket whose
path comes from env PRINTING_FFI_USB_FD_SOCK (the app serves the fd there when a
job is dispatched). Fallback for bench testing: a raw integer fd inherited from
the parent via env PRINTING_FFI_USB_FD.

When an fd is obtained, NO_DEVICE_DISCOVERY is set (before init) and the
enumerate+open path is replaced by libusb_wrap_sys_device(). conn (iface/altset/
endp_up/endp_down/bus/port) is derived from the wrapped handle's active config
descriptor, mirroring probe_device()'s endpoint-selection loop. Serial/URI
matching becomes advisory in this path (the app already picked the device it owns
the fd for).

All new code is guarded by #ifdef __ANDROID__ so desktop builds are unchanged.
This patch stays GPL (it patches the exec'd GPL backend); it is NOT copied into
the MIT plugin source.

